{
  "id": "2026-10-29-aiplatform-v1",
  "date": "2026-10-29",
  "api": "aiplatform.v1",
  "service": "Vertex AI",
  "title": "Vertex AI: File Management & Breaking Changes",
  "summary": "This update introduces significant breaking changes by making several parameters strictly required and certain properties read-only. Crucially, new APIs for file management and batch content embedding are now available, alongside enhancements for video generation experiments.",
  "details": "Heads up, developers! This is a breaking change release. The parameters 'name', 'parent', 'publishersId', and 'model' are now strictly required for various methods, necessitating updates to your API calls if you were previously omitting them. Additionally, several properties within the 'GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Agent' schema ('aiApplication') and 'GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ClaudeFile' schema ('created_at', 'downloadable', 'expires_at', 'filename', 'id', 'mime_type', 'size_bytes', 'type') have been made read-only. Ensure your code does not attempt to set these values.\n\nOn the feature front, a major addition is the new file management API under 'projects.locations.publishers.files', providing methods to 'create', 'get', 'list', 'delete', 'upload', and 'download' files, leveraging the new 'GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ClaudeFile' schema. This enables programmatic management of files for your AI applications. For embedding workflows, the new 'projects.locations.publishers.models.batchEmbedContents' method allows for efficient processing of multiple content items in a single request. Furthermore, 'CloudAiLargeModelsVisionGenerateVideoExperiments' gains new 'perfEstimationConfig' and 'superResConfig.steps' for more granular control over video generation experiments. Finally, 'projects.locations.agents.create' now accepts an 'idpNonce' parameter, and 'GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GenerateContentRequest' includes 'continuationToken' and 'outputConfig' for enhanced content generation control.",
  "impact": "high",
  "breaking": true,
  "interesting_score": 9,
  "tags": [
    "AI/ML",
    "Vertex AI",
    "Breaking Change",
    "New Features",
    "API"
  ],
